### Academic & Forensic Attribution Notice

The methodologies integrated into Subtext Engine are grounded in published, peer-reviewed scientific research, public judicial standards, and declassified defense frameworks:
- Criteria-Based Content Analysis (CBCA) © Max Steller & Günter Köhnken (1989).
- Statement Analysis Techniques © Susan H. Adams (FBI Law Enforcement Bulletin, 1996) and Mark McClish (Advanced Interviewing Concepts).
- Forensic Investigative Discourse Analysis © Malcolm Coulthard & John Olsson (2007, 2008).
- Linguistic Inquiry and Word Count (LIWC) © James W. Pennebaker & Matthew L. Newman (2003, 2011).
- Reality Monitoring in Deception Detection © Marcia K. Johnson, Carol L. Raye (1981) and Siegfried L. Sporer (2004).
- The B.I.T.E. Model of Authoritarian Control © Steven Hassan, Ph.D. (Freedom of Mind Resource Center).
- Chart of Coercion © Albert D. Biderman (Bulletin of the New York Academy of Medicine, 1957; Amnesty International).
- Interpersonal Deception Theory (IDT) © David B. Buller & Judee K. Burgoon (1996).
- Reflexive Control Theory © Vladimir A. Lefebvre (Institute of Psychology, USSR Academy of Sciences, 1967, 1982).
- Combined Motor Diagnosis of Conflict © Alexander R. Luria (1932).
- Theory of Suggestion & Counter-Suggestion © Boris F. Porshnev (1966, 1979).
- Italian Cognitive Forensics & Chronometric Latency © Giuseppe Sartori (University of Padua, 2008).
- Affective Mimicry & Emotional Deception © Stephen Porter (University of British Columbia, 2012).
- Global Statement Evaluation System (SEG/SRA) © Ramón Arce & Francisca Fariña (ALPJF, 2015).
- Strategic Use of Evidence (SUE) © Mark R. Kebbell & Neil Brewer (2005).
- Cross-Cultural Baseline Calibration © Alicia Nortje (University of Cape Town, 2019).
- Moscow Psycholinguistic School, Speech Activity & Predicate Hierarchies © Aleksei A. Leontiev, Yevgeny F. Tarasov, Tamara M. Dridze, Natalia V. Ufimtseva (Institute of Linguistics, USSR/Russian Academy of Sciences, 1974, 1976, 1990, 2011).
- Forensic Jurislinguistics, Implicit Meaning Analysis & Interrogation Profiling © Iosif A. Sternin, Anatoly N. Baranov, Vadim B. Chelpanov, Galina A. Kopnina, Aleksandr R. Ratinov (Voronezh State University, Institute of the Russian Language RAS, MAIL, Academy of the General Prosecutor's Office, 1967–2018).

All trademarks, registered names, and institutional affiliations belong to their respective holders. This software and documentation are provided strictly for academic, educational, analytical, and discourse-verification purposes.
